059-7c66148c781c" class="r-gcs1uv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h1><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I'm a Naturopathic Doctor Who Helps Women Transition Off Birth Control. Here's What I've Learned.</span></h1></span></div><div data-rid="23593667-9015-4411-9570-4acd28b917c4" class="r-j6t6l alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h1><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Stanford Dermatologist Reveals</span></h1><h1><mark data-color="#F1E77CFF" style="background-color: #F1E77CFF; color: inherit">Why Menopause Can Take 60,000 Hairs Before You Notice</mark><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> And </span><mark data-color="#FFFFFFFF" style="background-color: #FFFFFFFF; color: inherit">How You Can Prevent It At-Home In Under a Minute</mark></h1></span></div><picture data-rid="a91dbeaf-b774-4d1c-ac3e-8f86bc3aa24f" class="r-1br9wy6"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/e526e8be-7acc-456f-ace3-d5e6cbf5802b?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/d20ee3f2-4c51-4c94-b523-51a39c091e1b?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/d20ee3f2-4c51-4c94-b523-51a39c091e1b?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/d20ee3f2-4c51-4c94-b523-51a39c091e1b" class="r-155p76t" loading="eager"/></picture><div data-rid="fdb43e89-560e-4f69-ade7-ba041d63cba3" class="r-117x0b3 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h4><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">By Ashley Florestal, </span></strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Women's Health</span><br><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Focused, Certified Naturopathic Doctor</span></em></h4></span></div></div><div class="r-982yio" data-rid="1"><div data-rid="674cd535-cc49-4006-b4e8-16982bd747f1" class="r-hx4ihd"><div data-rid="47250868-cfd7-4cf3-af04-e8905518b5a2" class="r-1xtaue6"><div data-rid="c4af0c5d-e9f6-4247-893c-178491f5e175" class="r-uk6kj5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">For 5 years, I've focused in women's health, with a particular focus on supporting women through hormonal transitions.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">One of the most common challenges I see in my practice? Women who want to stop taking birth control but are terrified of what might happen when they do.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Their fears are valid. And having over 2500 patient visits, I've discovered why the transition can be so difficult—and what actually helps.</span><br></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="0f2a18ab-fb15-4ec6-9ed6-0a6eb9c18f52" class="r-ue97b6"><div data-rid="7be0f46a-f5bb-4efe-af8f-b3408958c48b" class="r-1wl90xb alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">The Birth Control Reality No One Talks About</span></strong></h2></span></div><picture data-rid="18a38416-4001-46fa-95b4-da626e46f7b7" class="r-8ath3b"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/0ed26840-60ce-483b-9bd3-7d4cc310a035?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/260bc872-50b3-4ce3-a2ed-6a0e157f1190?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/260bc872-50b3-4ce3-a2ed-6a0e157f1190?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/260bc872-50b3-4ce3-a2ed-6a0e157f1190" alt="Person with long hair holding their head with both hands." class="r-1b0fiu0" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="5b55742a-7404-4779-872c-0afe234198c6" class="r-lv9no0 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Birth control pills are remarkable. They've given women control over their reproductive health, helped manage painful periods, cleared stubborn acne, and provided reliable contraception.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">For many women, they're life-changing.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">But here's what often goes unmentioned: In one US study, researchers found that up to 58% of women who use hormonal contraceptives do so not only for pregnancy prevention but also for other health benefits, with period pain being one of the top motivations.*</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Another study revealed that oral contraceptives can deplete certain micronutrients, including B vitamins, vitamin C, vitamin E, magnesium, selenium, and zinc.*</span></p><p><br><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">When women decide to stop taking birth control—whether to conceive, due to side effects, or simply wanting to reconnect with their natural cycle—they often face an uncomfortable truth: the symptoms that drove them to birth control in the first place typically return.</span></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="93964618-625d-47d3-8242-61b508860c14" class="r-ggl08f"><div data-rid="71640c6a-7a2e-4a64-a794-ff763e54001d" class="r-18niort alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Why Your Pre-Pill Symptoms Come Back</span></strong></h2></span></div><picture data-rid="6bfe463e-b69a-4c5b-a3c4-649beeefa204" class="r-ya5qr4"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/a1ac4b9d-182b-48e9-ad00-be58332e7cc8?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/7ec6ab84-e1ad-49e6-8b73-d7bec52688d5?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/7ec6ab84-e1ad-49e6-8b73-d7bec52688d5?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/7ec6ab84-e1ad-49e6-8b73-d7bec52688d5" class="r-2kl8q" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="ad461519-9461-4569-aa5c-dc0f1e9231cf" class="r-1bga20o alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">It makes sense when you think about it. Birth control doesn't cure the underlying causes of painful periods, acne, or irregular cycles.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">It manages these symptoms by overriding your natural hormonal fluctuations with synthetic hormones.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">So when you stop? Your body returns to its pre-contraceptive state. For some women, this transition is smooth. But for many others, it means dealing with:</span></p><br><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">The return of painful periods</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Skin breakouts</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Irregular cycles</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Mood swings</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Bloating</span></p><br></li></ul><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Some women even experience temporary "flare-ups" where symptoms feel worse than before they started birth control, as their body readjusts to producing its own hormones again.</span></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="6c81376a-bdc9-4a92-ae32-a8624ff145ae" class="r-1f5451s"><div data-rid="eafcb9bc-2a8f-4228-a403-7c05b5a9f342" class="r-1iu2aip alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">What I've Observed in My Practice</span></strong></h2></span></div><picture data-rid="a6ce6e2c-d1be-4c21-8fea-e0eaa31b9067" class="r-u09121"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/732fff0e-676f-4ed8-9573-2948429fdfad?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/7ec6ab84-e1ad-49e6-8b73-d7bec52688d5?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/7ec6ab84-e1ad-49e6-8b73-d7bec52688d5?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/7ec6ab84-e1ad-49e6-8b73-d7bec52688d5" class="r-1p1qew1" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="834c3289-39a4-46f9-96e5-dcc36e16cdec" class="r-6jgegw alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Through my years of practice, I've observed an interesting pattern.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Many women who seem to have smoother transitions off birth control are those who prepare their bodies with nutritional support beforehand.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">They often work on addressing potential imbalances before stopping, focus on replenishing nutrients, and support their body's hormone production throughout the process.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">From what I've seen, women who tend to struggle more are often those who stop suddenly without preparation or support, hoping their bodies will naturally adjust on their own.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">These observations have influenced how I approach supporting women through this transition, and I've had the opportunity to help many women navigate this change more comfortably.</span></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="949b0b9e-2b65-4324-b828-50b0e3d14e5d" class="r-ex14v7"><div data-rid="b39bc8ad-f1c2-40ab-915d-c4cb0a2e2982" class="r-mlweru alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">The Missing Piece: Targeted Nutritional Support</span></strong></h2></span></div><picture data-rid="51277d09-e54e-4455-ad95-eb4a816c4c72" class="r-1sdr74d"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/1b804598-2798-4fd6-bcbb-d1d537cddd03?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/6b368814-8181-4e42-a34f-d610fcc0c7fd?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/6b368814-8181-4e42-a34f-d610fcc0c7fd?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/6b368814-8181-4e42-a34f-d610fcc0c7fd" class="r-11epoz2" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="a3c0042e-e102-49f7-871a-e580c1a95f7e" class="r-1y5sex alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">The key insight? Your body can benefit from specific nutritional support during this transition period. </span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Remember those nutrient depletions I mentioned? They're part of the puzzle.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">When we address prostaglandins while simultaneously replenishing nutrients and supporting your body's natural hormone production, the transition becomes much more manageable.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">This is where monthlies comes in.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">It's a comprehensive nutritional supplement I recommend to women who are planning to transition off birth control and are concerned about their period pain or premenstrual symptoms coming back.</span></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="9d5e543a-9ee1-4c19-bf0f-984f581f1b70" class="r-1lo9e2z"><div data-rid="1818ac84-cf52-475d-94e0-1c706b3644e7" class="r-1g0d0fo alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">The Science Behind the Solution</span></strong></h2></span></div><picture data-rid="5d6eabda-a05f-4386-a071-3a891fcc5366" class="r-nm9aa1"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0708/7462/8371/files/2_6.webp?v=1737644053&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/d802e264-6ba1-4f68-b2da-53efb38d7a00?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/d802e264-6ba1-4f68-b2da-53efb38d7a00?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/74ef5866-9ad7-456b-81d4-5e84e591ae16/d802e264-6ba1-4f68-b2da-53efb38d7a00" alt="Doctor examining a woman&#x27;s face in a clinic setting." class="r-kx2arl" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="8a459c38-fca6-41f5-9431-2d56531d127a" class="r-1f3ixwd alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">monthlies contains evidence-based ingredients that address period pain at its source:</span></p></span></div><div data-rid="5e6c01cd-abbd-49db-8be7-0d676e61ede0" class="r-szn42v"><div data-rid="c9cb3487-6472-488d-a8a5-a07aa0856413" class="r-19vcan9"><picture data-rid="b4a122af-b87f-4f21-b0be-765301b5f50d" class="r-eflmlq"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/7fe51a3b-4fc6-40c5-9a43-29238b8bb09d?width=100" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0771/0860/9337/files/Kuru_17.webp?v=1724611480&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0771/0860/9337/files/Kuru_17.webp?v=1724611480&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0771/0860/9337/files/Kuru_17.webp?v=1724611480" alt="Close-up of green mint leaves in a garden." class="r-1vajyu1" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div data-rid="e3a1780a-db83-4ec6-b182-5c3ab7b9c944" class="r-21ryf0 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Ginger</span></strong></p></span></div><div data-rid="6eddfc39-8cec-48c9-a84a-802e50fe1de4" class="r-184kbma alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">In one study, 2 grams of ginger was shown to be as effective as mefenamic acid (a common NSAID) for reducing menstrual pain intensity.*</span></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="256aa3b0-4e0e-4960-a013-a7f3b11a7805" class="r-1nlubox"><div data-rid="a0e80bf3-ba30-4307-8d2d-2969f4f45835" class="r-epyz16"><picture data-rid="95234da1-c812-4e2f-99b1-13d7e7a30560" class="r-1uqetaj"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/05d1c41a-8cc0-4d37-87de-b42dfbdbefe9/14f6baf7-1879-4d44-a50e-23524be93acb?width=100" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0771/0860/9337/files/Kuru_17.webp?v=1724611480&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0771/0860/9337/files/Kuru_17.webp?v=1724611480&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0771/0860/9337/files/Kuru_17.webp?v=1724611480" alt="Close-up of green mint leaves in a garden." class="r-1p4skss" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div data-rid="bfcd34bf-6091-480a-92d7-c444a3b71e88" class="r-jxerwp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Zinc</span></strong></p></span></div><div data-rid="63bcee80-bf80-4cdd-9406-e5c04b60c09d" class="r-1k6jsv5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Research indicates that zinc supplementation can significantly reduce the severity of primary dysmenorrhea. Studies have also shown zin